{{- /*
  jira/access-method — canonical "JIRA MCP tools vs `jira` CLI" preamble:
  the "prefer MCP tools whenever available" framing, the
  {{ if Cond "Tools.Names.exists(n, n.matches('(?i)jira'))" }} branch, and the
  full canonical-operation → CLI-command mapping table (ankitpokhrel/jira-cli).
  Extracted per mitto-w8jp.2 from new-ticket, push-issue, pull-issue and
  sync-tasks, which shipped four near-identical copies (new-ticket carried the
  richest CLI table; the other three had a narrower prose-only version). A
  mismatch here means one prompt calls a CLI flag another prompt already knows
  is wrong, so this fragment is the single source of truth for the mapping.

  Callers pass a dict:
    "Note" — a short caller-specific sentence naming which of its own steps
             the JIRA operations live in (e.g. "the transitions tools in
             Step 3 and the add-comment tool in Step 4"). Rendered after the
             branch, in both the MCP and CLI cases. Optional — omit for a
             generic closing sentence.

  Usage:

      {{ template "jira/shared/access-method"
           (dict "Note" "the transitions tools in Step 3 and the add-comment tool in Step 4") }}
*/ -}}
{{- $note := .Note -}}
This prompt talks to JIRA in one of two ways: **JIRA MCP tools** (e.g. `jira_get_issue_jira`, `jira_search_jira`, `jira_get_transitions`, `jira_transition_issue`, `jira_add_comment`, `jira_create_issue_jira`) or the **`jira` CLI** (ankitpokhrel/jira-cli). **Prefer MCP tools whenever they are available** — they return structured JSON, avoid a subprocess round-trip, and do not depend on the user's local `jira` config. Fall back to the CLI only when the matching MCP tool is not present.
{{ if Cond "Tools.Names.exists(n, n.matches('(?i)jira'))" -}}
**This run has JIRA MCP tools available** (a tool whose name contains `jira` is reachable). Every JIRA read/write below should go through the MCP tool named in the step{{ if $note }} ({{ $note }}){{ end }}. Names may be namespaced by the client (`mcp__<server>__<op>`); prefer whichever exact name is exposed to you. Use the CLI only for a specific operation whose MCP counterpart genuinely is not exposed by this workspace's server; do not mix the two for the same call.
{{- else }}
**This run has no JIRA MCP tools** (no tool name contains `jira`) but the `jira` command is on PATH — use it as the fallback. Wherever a step names an MCP tool, run the CLI equivalent instead{{ if $note }} ({{ $note }}){{ end }}. Set `PAGER=cat` before any `jira issue view` to bypass the pager.

| Canonical operation | `jira` CLI command |
|---|---|
| `jira_get_agile_boards_jira` | `jira board list` |
| `jira_get_sprints_from_board_jira` (active) | `jira sprint list --state active --table --plain --columns id,name,state` — take the active sprint's id |
| `jira_search_jira` (JQL) | `jira issue list -q "<JQL>" --plain --no-headers` (append `--raw` for JSON, `--paginate <N>` to raise the result cap). `currentUser()` works inside JQL |
| `jira_get_issue_jira` (single ticket) | `jira issue list -q "key = <KEY>" --raw` |
| `jira_get_comments_jira` / per-issue comments | `PAGER=cat jira issue view <KEY> --comments <N>` |
| `jira_get_filter` (saved filter) | `jira filter view <ID>` |
| `jira_get_server_info_jira` | no equivalent — `jira me` confirms auth/identity; the base URL lives in your jira config |
| `jira_create_issue_jira` | `jira issue create -p<PROJECT> -t<TYPE> -s"<summary>" -y<PRIORITY> -l<label> -C<component> --template <desc.md> --no-input` |
| `jira_assign_issue_jira` | `jira issue assign <KEY> "<user>"` (self: `$(jira me)`; unassign: `x`) |
| `jira_add_issues_to_sprint_jira` | `jira sprint add <SPRINT_ID> <KEY>` |
| `jira_get_transitions_jira` + `jira_transition_issue_jira` | `jira issue transitions <KEY>` to list, then `jira issue move <KEY> "<name>"` to apply |
| `jira_add_comment` | `jira issue comment add <KEY> --body-file <path>` |
| `jira_get_link_types_jira` + `jira_create_issue_link_jira` | `jira issue link <KEY> <TARGET_KEY> <LinkType>` (e.g. `Blocks`, `Relates`) |

CLI notes:
- Pass `--no-input` on `create`/`assign`/`move` so they never block on the interactive TUI; use `--plain`/`--raw` on `list` for the same reason.
- Write the Markdown description/comment body to a temp file and pass it via `--template <file>` / `--body-file <file>` — do not inline multi-line text on the command line.
- Labels/components repeat the flag (`-lbug -lurgent`, `-CBackend`); priority is `-yHigh`; attach to an epic/parent with `-P<EPIC-KEY>`.
- Comment bodies may be omitted from `list --raw` on JIRA Server / Data Center; fetch them per ticket with `jira issue view <KEY> --comments <N>` instead.
{{- end }}
